        "original_id": "ecb0cb54-48d9-5ae4-ab0c-795a28306d34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thornton Wilder, Richard Llewellyn, Huw Morgan\n- Works: The Long Christmas Dinner, How Green Was My Valley\n- Roles: American playwright, American novelist, British novelist\n- Topics: Welsh family, mining community\n\nFacts:\n- Thornton Wilder was born on April 17, 1897, and he was an American playwright and novelist.\n- Richard Llewellyn, born Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd, was born on December 8, 1906, and he was a British novelist.\n- Thornton Wilder wrote the one-act play The Long Christmas Dinner in 1931.\n- Richard Llewellyn published the novel How Green Was My Valley in 1939.\n- How Green Was My Valley is narrated by Huw Morgan, its main character.\n- How Green Was My Valley is about a Welsh family and the mining community in which they live.\n- Thornton Wilder died on December 7, 1975.\n- Richard Llewellyn died on November 30, 1983.",
